# Code owners for this repository.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owners of every path a pull request touches. With
# 'require_code_owner_review' enabled in the master ruleset, that review is also required before
# the pull request can merge.
#
# Rules are matched in order and the LAST matching rule wins, so a later, more specific line
# overrides the catch-all above it. Patterns follow .gitignore syntax.

# Everything, unless a rule below overrides it.
*                          @DarkVader0

# How the repository is built, tested and measured. Called out separately because a change here
# governs every project in the repository rather than any one of them: RemoteBuildTool's own hash
# folds into every target's fullHash (see RemoteBuildToolVersion in src/RemoteBuildTool/Bitenovac.RemoteBuildTool), so a change
# here invalidates the whole cache, and the reviewer should be someone who knows why.
/src/RemoteBuildTool/       @DarkVader0
/.github/                  @DarkVader0
/runner/*.sh               @DarkVader0
/docker/                   @DarkVader0
/Directory.Build.props     @DarkVader0
/Directory.Build.targets   @DarkVader0
/Directory.Packages.props  @DarkVader0
/global.json               @DarkVader0
/nuget.config               @DarkVader0

# The decompression algorithms themselves. Getting these wrong is a diver safety issue, not a
# build failure, so they are worth naming explicitly once there is more than one maintainer.
/src/DecompressionAlgorithms/  @DarkVader0
/src/DecompressionCalculator/  @DarkVader0
